  "body": "**Link to problem area**:\r\nhttps://spec.matrix.org/latest/appendices/#room-ids\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n- According to https://matrix.to/#/%23urandom%3Amaunium.net/%24GC76GPFSf0n8VEHdZN2FxSgiRb2MGDcA6L0DRwAVR7s?via=sosnowkadub.de&via=exkc.moe&via=synapse.test.progval.net&via=ucmeet-server.business.celcom.com.my Room IDs need to be limited to 255 chars to be valid in state keys\r\n- these 255 chars probably apply to URL encoded ASCII representation because room IDs get used in URIs? I'm not sure. it seems strange that character-set, encoding, etc appears to not be defined while user IDs at least speak of UTF-8 and explicitly state a 255 char limit.",
